# Research Gap

Student 2 - Khushi Agarwal
The literature survey shows that most existing research focuses on demand forecasting, customer behaviour analysis, business intelligence, and intelligent decision-making using Artificial Intelligence. Although these approaches improve prediction accuracy and business operations, they do not solve the problem of intelligent cloud resource management during sudden traffic spikes.

Traditional cloud auto-scaling techniques mainly depend on fixed threshold values such as CPU utilization or memory usage. These rule-based methods cannot efficiently handle unpredictable workload changes during e-commerce festival sales. As a result, they may cause high response time, server overload, poor user experience, and increased cloud infrastructure costs.

Very few studies combine Reinforcement Learning with AWS cloud services to make intelligent real-time scaling decisions. Existing research also lacks an adaptive framework that continuously learns from changing workloads and automatically allocates cloud resources.

To overcome these limitations, this project proposes an **Intelligent Cloud Auto-Scaling Framework for E-Commerce Festival Sales Using Reinforcement Learning**. The proposed system continuously monitors cloud performance metrics, learns workload patterns using Reinforcement Learning, and automatically scales cloud resources based on real-time demand. This approach improves application performance, ensures high availability during peak traffic, and reduces operational costs through efficient resource utilization.